    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_2",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Rich Banner and Frank Chadwick formed the ISU Game Club at the Illinois State University (Normal, Illinois). Banner engineered a grant which funded the printing of blank hex sheets (suitable for making wargame maps) and all three began drafting a variety of designs, some derivative of existing games at the time, and some original concepts.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
